     "summary": "prose fingerprints every heading and non-requirement, non-history sentence with code spans blanked, then every fenced-block line without trailing whitespace.",
     "rationale": "The requirement-word heuristic cannot see every rule, so any prose change asks for review (X1). Fenced blocks were left out as commands, so a rule written only in a fence was invisible; now an edit inside a fence flags the claim. Inline code spans stay blanked, so inline command edits stay quiet. The cost is one review and re-pin for a command-only fence edit, which is a review, not a red verdict. Verified by TestPinFlagsProseChangesButNotCommands, TestDatedRulesAndFencedBlocksFlagClaimForReview and the claims.md drive (cl-fence, cl-fence-pinned, cl-fence-edit). Fences opened with ~~~ are not fences to the parser, so their lines count as ordinary sentences and still flag.",
     "author": "fm/verilex-claim-model"
    },
    {
     "newRange": [
      155,
      239
     ],
     "summary": "subFeature collects a heading named by the id plus every list item, paragraph or table row that opens with the id in code.",
     "rationale": "Runbooks rarely state which step proves which sub-feature (R19), so the scope must be explicit: a step labelled with its id. A lazy continuation line that starts with the id is a mention, not a block. A list item keeps nested lines and fences, so prose sees a fence nested under the step.",
     "author": "fm/verilex-claim-model"
    },
    {
     "newRange": [
      241,
      290
     ],
     "summary": "runHistory leaves out only a sentence that opens with YYYY-MM-DD: or Verified YYYY-MM-DD:, after an optional sub-feature label.",
     "rationale": "Any sentence with an ISO date used to count as run history, so a dated rule such as 'Since 2026-10-01 a NAME added twice must exit 2.' flagged nothing and the chain skipped. Now every other dated sentence is a requirement or prose like the rest, so a dated rule reports 'requirement no claim maps'. ReadClaim still refuses a mapped run-history sentence. Verified by TestDatedRulesAndFencedBlocksFlagClaimForReview, the featuremap unit cases, and the claims.md drive (cl-dated, cl-history).",
     "author": "fm/verilex-claim-model"
    }
   ]
